course: dictionary
lesson: 11051
title: Wednesday, the middle of the week
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wednesday is a day of the week. It comes after Tuesday and before Thursday, so it sits in the middle of the school week. «One Wednesday Jayden saw Zara watching from the side, quiet.» Here Wednesday names one particular day.
explain: Context helps you spot the day. In the story, the days run in order: «Mr Hughes has a cold» on Monday, «Mr Hughes is really ill» on Tuesday, and «Mr Hughes is in hospital» on Wednesday. Wednesday is the third day, so you can find it by counting along the week.
explain: Notice the capital W, because days always start with a capital letter. Add an s to make Wednesdays, which means every Wednesday, like a club that meets each week on Wednesdays. «By Wednesday somebody has drawn a chicken on Sam's pencil case» shows how a day can be the turning point of a story.
fact: Wednesday is the day of the week after Tuesday and before Thursday.
fact: Wednesday is in the middle of the school week, so people call it «midweek».
fact: Add an s to make «Wednesdays», which means every Wednesday.
fact: In French, Wednesday is «mercredi», and the days are lundi, mardi, mercredi, jeudi, vendredi, samedi and dimanche.
fact: Days of the week always start with a capital letter: Wednesday, not wednesday.
exercise: Which day comes straight after Tuesday and before Thursday? | Sunday | *Wednesday | Monday | Friday
exercise: In the story, on which day does «Mr Hughes is in hospital» happen? | Thursday | Tuesday | Monday | *Wednesday
exercise: A club meets on the same day every week. Which word shows it is every week? | *Wednesdays | Wednesday | Thursday | Midweek
test: In French, «mercredi» means which day? | Friday | *Wednesday | Thursday | Monday
test: Mia says Wednesday is the last day of the school week. What is the right answer? | It is the weekend | *It is in the middle of the school week | It is the first day of the week | It comes after Friday
exam: Which word means every week, as in «swimming is on …» for a club that meets each week? | Midweek | Weekend | *Wednesdays | Wednesday
